>> title: Almond Croissant
>> category: Pastry & Doughs
>> tags: pastry, almond, laminated, second-bake, oven
>> counters: Bakery
>> aka: almond croissant, croissant aux amandes, croissant amandine, twice-baked croissant, frangipane croissant
>> pairs-with: croissant, frangipane
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr 15 min
>> step.1: boil the syrup, cool it
>> step.2: halve the croissants and soak the cut sides
>> step.3: pipe the filling in and close them
>> step.4: top, scatter almonds, bake 350°F (175°C) 20 min
>> step.5: dust once they are cool

Boil @water{1/2%cup}(120 mL) with @granulated sugar{1/3%cup}(70 g) and @dark rum{1%Tbs}(15 mL) until the sugar has gone, then ~cool{15%min} to lukewarm.

Split @day-old croissants{6}(a day old, or two — fresh ones collapse) in half through the middle and brush the cut faces generously with @&(~1)syrup{}.

Pipe @frangipane{3/4%cup}(200 g) onto @&(~1)soaked bottoms{} in a thick spiral and set the tops back on.

Spread @frangipane{1/4%cup}(70 g) over @&(~1)filled croissants{}, scatter @sliced almonds{1/2%cup}(45 g) over, and bake on a lined tray in a 350°F (175°C) #oven{} ~bake{20%min}, until the filling has set.

Dust @&(~1)baked croissants{} with @powdered sugar{2%Tbs}(15 g) once they are cool.
